    file: "FKS_Financial_Your_Contract_Your_Protection.docx",
    text: "YOUR CONTRACT. YOUR PROTECTION. YOUR DECISION.\nUNDERSTANDING YOUR POLICY\nWhen you purchase an insurance policy, the contract is between you and the company that issues it. Take the time to understand the company, the policy, and the responsibilities involved.\nKNOW WHAT THE CONTRACT SAYS\nYour coverage and premiums\nPolicy benefits and eligibility\nConditions, limits, and exclusions\nCash-value provisions, when applicable\nYour rights and responsibilities\nThe insurance company’s contractual obligations\nASK BEFORE YOU DECIDE\nA verbal explanation does not replace your policy. Ask questions, review the numbers, and read the terms before making a decision.\nCONTACTING THE COMPANY\nUse the customer-service information supplied with your policy when you need help from the issuing insurer.\nEDUCATIONAL NOTICE\nThis content is general information. Policy features and availability vary. Consult an appropriately licensed professional about your circumstances.",
